From 3228507b235aed4bdcf79beebbff47ae04a69a9d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@users.invalid>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 04:32:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/10] VPVulkan: per-submit fences, timeline semaphores,
 synchronization2 (no device-wide waits)

New src/sync.cpp. Every vkQueueSubmit/vkQueueSubmit2 is one core frame; its fence and semaphore
signals complete when the backend reports that frame finished. gpu/metal2 now implements
Backend::completedFrames (lowest frame still in flight, updated by the command buffer completion
handlers), so vkWaitForFences / vkGetFenceStatus / vkQueueWaitIdle / vkDeviceWaitIdle wait for
exactly the frames involved, honour timeouts and waitAll=false.

VK_KHR_timeline_semaphore: VkSemaphoreTypeCreateInfo, VkTimelineSemaphoreSubmitInfo,
vkGetSemaphoreCounterValue, vkWaitSemaphores (all/any, timeout), vkSignalSemaphore. A timeline
wait on a value no submission promised blocks the submitting thread until the host signals it
(wait-before-signal); binary waits never block (in-order queue; the host layer's synthesized
swapchain acquire never signals this driver's semaphores).
VK_KHR_synchronization2: vkQueueSubmit2, vkCmdPipelineBarrier2 (in-pass barriers feed local
read), vkCmdSet/Reset/WaitEvents2, vkCmdWriteTimestamp2. KHR aliases resolved.

Test: gpu_vulkan.sync (null backend holds frames unfinished).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
